# =============================================================================================== #
#  BAF HTCondor Job Template
# =============================================================================================== #
#  Copy this file, adjust the values below, and submit with:
#
#      >> condor_submit ~/scripts/job.jdl
#
#  Do NOT submit from /cephfs — run condor_submit from your home directory.
#  Put only large data / output files on CephFS for maximum performance.
# =============================================================================================== #

# -- Executable & Arguments --
executable          = /home/nklugeco/physik/scripts/train_ddp.sh
arguments           = $(ClusterId)

# -- Resource Requests --
request_cpus        = 48
request_memory      = 200000
request_disk        = 104857600
request_gpus        = 2

# -- Machine Selection --
requirements        = (CUDADeviceName == "NVIDIA H200")

# -- Container & Filesystem (BAF-specific) --
+ContainerOS        = "Rocky9"
+CephFS_IO          = "high"
+MaxRuntimeHours    = 4

# -- Logging & Output --
output              = /dev/null
error               = /dev/null
log                 = $(ClusterId).log

# -- Transfer --
# BUDDY is a shell env var (your CephFS home) that the script relies on for
# datadir; it must be explicitly whitelisted since we don't import the full
# submit-host environment.
getenv                = BUDDY
transfer_output_files = ""

# -- Submit exactly 1 instance of this job --
Queue 1
# =============================================================================================== #
#  REFERENCE — everything you need to know to submit jobs on BAF
# =============================================================================================== #

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- #
#  QUICK START: How to submit and monitor
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- #
#
#   Submit a batch job:
#     >> condor_submit job.jdl
#
#   Submit an interactive job (max 24 h):
#     >> condor_submit -interactive job.jdl
#
#   Check your jobs (all users, all submit hosts):
#     >> condor_q -all -global
#
#   Show only running jobs:
#     >> condor_q -constraint 'JobStatus == 2'
#
#   Show running jobs expanded (unfold arrays):
#     >> condor_q -nobatch
#
#   Find out why an IDLE job is not starting:
#     >> condor_q -better-analyze <JobID>
#
#   Tail stdout of a running job:
#     >> condor_tail -f <JobID>
#
#   Tail stderr of a running job:
#     >> condor_tail -stderr <JobID>
#
#   Kill / remove jobs:
#     >> condor_rm <ClusterID>          # specific cluster
#     >> condor_rm -all                 # all your jobs
#
#   Release held jobs:
#     >> condor_release <your-uni-id>
#
#   Check job resource usage (running jobs):
#     >> condor_q -constraint 'JobStatus == 2' -af:hj Cmd ResidentSetSize_RAW RequestMemory DiskUsage_RAW RequestDisk RequestCPUs CPUsUsage
#
#   Check resource usage of finished jobs:
#     >> condor_history -constraint 'JobStatus == 4' -af:hj Cmd ResidentSetSize_RAW RequestMemory DiskUsage_RAW RequestDisk
#
#   Check user priorities:
#     >> condor_userprio -allusers -all
#
#   Raise priority of your job by 10:
#     >> condor_prio -p 10 <JobID>
#
#   Edit resources of IDLE jobs (only JobStatus == 1):
#     >> condor_qedit <ClusterID> -constraint 'JobStatus == 1' RequestMemory 1500 RequestCpus 4
#
#   Tip: Use python -u for unbuffered stdout in Python jobs.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- #
#  CHECKING AVAILABLE RESOURCES
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- #
#
#   GPU machines and their free slots:
#     >> condor_status -compact -constraint 'GPUs > 0' -af:h Machine State GPUs Cpus Memory Disk CUDADeviceName
#
#   GPU machines — total vs. used resources:
#     >> condor_status -compact -constraint 'GPUs > 0' -af:h Machine State TotalGPUs GPUs TotalCpus Cpus TotalMemory Memory TotalDisk Disk CUDADeviceName
#
#   Available (idle) slots with free CPUs / Memory / CephFS capability:
#     >> condor_status -avail -af:h Name Memory Cpus CephFS_IO_Capability
#
#   Machine health and reboot status:
#     >> condor_status -compact -af:h Machine NODE_IS_HEALTHY StartJobs NODE_HEALTH MARKED_FOR_REBOOT NODE_REBOOT_REASONS NODE_REBOOT_ACTION DRAIN_FOR_REBOOT_AFTER 'formatTime(DRAIN_FOR_REBOOT_AFTER)'
#
#   Draining nodes and acceptable job lengths:
#     >> condor_status -compact -af:h Machine CPUs BackfillableMaxRuntimeHours 'formatTime(MaxLatestJobEndTime)' IMMEDIATE_DRAIN TIMED_DRAIN DRAIN_TARGET_TIME 'formatTime(DRAIN_TARGET_TIME)' DRAIN_REASONS
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- #
#  BAF SPECIAL ATTRIBUTES
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- #
#
#  +ContainerOS — operating system inside the container
#  ┌──────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┐
#  │ Value            │ Notes                                 │
#  ├──────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┤
#  │ "Debian13"       │ Latest Debian                         │
#  │ "Debian12"       │                                       │
#  │ "Debian11"       │                                       │
#  │ "Rocky9"         │ RHEL 9 compatible (recommended)       │
#  │ "Rocky8"         │ RHEL 8 compatible                     │
#  └──────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────┘
#
#  +CephFS_IO — I/O throughput class to /cephfs
#  ┌──────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
#  │ Value    │ Meaning                                                  │
#  ├──────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
#  │ "high"   │ Max throughput (56 GBit/s InfiniBand)                    │
#  │ "medium" │ Moderate (Ethernet, e.g. simulation output)              │
#  │ "low"    │ Minimal (status files, small text files)                 │
#  │ "none"   │ Job does not access /cephfs at all                       │
#  └──────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
#
#  +MaxRuntimeHours — maximum wallclock time per job
#  ┌─────────────────────┬──────────────────────┐
#  │ Job Type            │ Runtime Limit        │
#  ├─────────────────────┼──────────────────────┤
#  │ Interactive Job     │ 24 hours (max)       │
#  │ Batch Job           │ 7 days = 168 h (max) │
#  └─────────────────────┴──────────────────────┘
#  Shorter runtimes may let your job backfill draining nodes.
#  The job is killed if it exceeds this time — always include a safety margin.
#
#  Environment setup files (sourced automatically):
#    $BUDDY/.bashrc_Rocky9     $BUDDY/.bashrc_Debian13
#    $BUDDY/.bashrc_Rocky8     $BUDDY/.bashrc_Debian12
#                               $BUDDY/.bashrc_Debian11
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- #
#  GPU MACHINES — available hardware on BAF
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- #
#
#  ┌───────────────────┬──────────┬──────────┬──────────┬──────────┬──────────┐
#  │ CUDADeviceName    │ GPUs     │ CPUs     │ RAM      │ Disk     │ VRAM/GPU │
#  ├───────────────────┼──────────┼──────────┼──────────┼──────────┼──────────┤
#  │ "NVIDIA H200"     │ 8 total  │ 192      │ 2,322 GB │ ~ 3.3 TB │ 141 GB   │
#  │ "NVIDIA H100 PCIe"│ 2 total  │ 128      │ 2,064 GB │ ~ 6.6 TB │ 80 GB    │
#  └───────────────────┴──────────┴──────────┴──────────┴──────────┴──────────┘
#
#  When changing request_gpus, also update CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES and
#  --nproc_per_node in your job script to match.
#
#  CPU cores per GPU (approx):  H200 → 24  |  H100 → 64
#  (Divide TotalCpus by TotalGPUs for your allocation.)
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- #
#  IMPORTANT NOTES
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- #
#
#  * Only the "vanilla" universe is supported (no MPI / parallel universe).
#  * Do NOT submit from /cephfs — use your home directory.
#  * Do NOT put CephFS files in transfer_input_files / transfer_output_files.
#  * HTCondor transfers back all files in the job working directory (/jwd).
#    Put temporary files in a subdirectory of /jwd to avoid this.
#  * The executable is copied as condor_exec.exe, so $0 is not the original
#    script name inside the job.
#  * set -e is recommended in scripts — but do NOT use it before setupATLAS.
#  * For jobs > 24 h or large queues, prolong your Kerberos TGT:
#    https://confluence.team.uni-bonn.de/spaces/PHYIT/pages/17011120/Prolonging+Kerberos+TGTs
#  * Interactive jobs block resources — do not keep shells open unnecessarily.
#  * Full BAF HTCondor docs:
#    https://confluence.team.uni-bonn.de/spaces/PHYIT/pages/10814633/HTCondor+on+BAF
#  * GPU-specific docs:
#    https://confluence.team.uni-bonn.de/spaces/PHYIT/pages/12289903/HTCondor+GPU+jobs
#  * Helpful commands cheatsheet:
#    https://confluence.team.uni-bonn.de/spaces/PHYIT/pages/10814637/Helpful+HTCondor+commands
#
# =============================================================================================== #
